st need  to check in are you still telling that  lie are you telling new lies  wait are we talking about i'm sorry  david are we talking about do you want  to talk about something completely  non-related and try to catch me on a  monday morning totally off topic or do  you want to talk about elon musk  i just love the reference from the host  to monday morning david lit you know  on a tuesday afternoon this would be  acceptable  how dare you try this on me on a monday  morning and this is actually something  that's done really frequently  when a host is pushed up against a wall  or made uncomfortable they often will go  back to  this isn't what we booked you to talk  about i've sometimes done this as a  guest sometimes guests when the guest is  sandbagged  the guest will say you didn't book me to  talk about this  and it's a rhetorical crutch you just  have to be prepared for how to handle it  unless you've agreed not to talk about  something  you just have to be prepared as the host  or as the guest  i've had situations we've had maybe two  or three situations where a guest  or their publicist will say listen  please don't  ask about x because there's ongoing  litigation  just can't comment on it and it's going  to bring the interview to a halt and of  course  i have the option as the host of saying  well i will ask about it but the guest  can say i'm not able to to talk about  that right now  or it might not even really be a central  topic and i would say oh yeah that's not  the topic of the interview anyway  i've been on shows where they give me a  list of eight topics and say we might  talk about these things  and i have said before i don't know  anything about topic number five  so i'd rather not talk about it if you  ask me i'll just say i don't know about  that so i'm not the right person to ask  and we sort of come to an agreement  other than that it's basically just a  rhetorical game  and sometimes when a guest will turn  around and start asking the host  